{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Eastern Europe. Housing estate life. Full-time work. Exhaustion. And where does all this lead?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The goal is to get home every day and sleep, so you can get rid of your hallucinations.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game ends when you have found all the anomalies.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Observe your surroundings carefully to get home.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Don't miss any changes!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you find an anomaly, press the RED button in the elevator.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you don't find an anomaly, press the GREEN button.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;When will I get Home?&quot; is an anomaly-finding walking simulator inspired by my own staircases.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game is only available in English, but if you understand the simple game mechanics above, you can easily play through it without knowing the language.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Playtime:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >30-120 minutes</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Settings:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game always starts in the native desktop resolution. Scalable graphics settings allow you to increase performance, mouse sensitivity, and volume.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/4087740?t=1762839658","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/4087740?t=1762839658","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4087740/9ab6462da49c4244c2ee6459962991e65aa0d0ca/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1762839658","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4087740/9ab6462da49c4244c2ee6459962991e65aa0d0ca/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1762839658","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Eastern Europe. Housing estate life. Full-time work. Exhaustion. And where does all this lead?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The goal is to get home every day and sleep, so you can get rid of your hallucinations.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game ends when you have found all the anomalies.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Observe your surroundings carefully to get home.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Don't miss any changes!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you find an anomaly, press the RED button in the elevator.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you don't find an anomaly, press the GREEN button.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;When will I get Home?&quot; is an anomaly-finding walking simulator inspired by my own staircases.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game is only available in English, but if you understand the simple game mechanics above, you can easily play through it without knowing the language.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Playtime:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >30-120 minutes</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Settings:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game always starts in the native desktop resolution. Scalable graphics settings allow you to increase performance, mouse sensitivity, and volume.</p>","developers":["ZForgeGames"],"genres":[{"description":"Indie","id":"23"},{"description":"Simulation","id":"28"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4087740/c999e0bcf64b304acea8e98aa5f74efc7dd0e4be/header.jpg?t=1762839658","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":[],"mac_requirements":[],"movies":[{"dash_av1":"https://video.akama